# Copy to .env (gitignored — never commit real credentials) in this same directory. Read fresh
# per call by EnvConfig, keyed to this tool's own name ('bitbucket-deploy-logs') — not shared with
# any other tool's .env, even bitbucket-open-pr's.

# Basic-auth credentials for the Bitbucket Cloud REST API: an Atlassian account email plus an API
# token generated at id.atlassian.com (Security -> API tokens). The token needs read access to
# Pipelines on whatever repositories this profile will be used against. Which env var pair belongs
# to which authProfile is declared in auth-profiles.json — add a new pair here and a matching
# entry there for another Bitbucket account/profile, rather than reusing this one.
DEPLOY_LOGS_EXAMPLE_PROFILE_EMAIL="you@example.com"
DEPLOY_LOGS_EXAMPLE_PROFILE_API_TOKEN="your-atlassian-api-token"
